1
00:00:03,185 --> 00:00:08,838
On the Soft Phone tab, the Default telephony provider lists every provider you turned on.

2
00:00:08,838 --> 00:00:12,885
The soft phone places and controls its calls through this one.

3
00:00:13,338 --> 00:00:17,909
Allowed short codes lists short numbers people may dial, one per line, such

4
00:00:17,909 --> 00:00:19,828
as a carrier service number.

5
00:00:19,828 --> 00:00:22,931
Short numbers are refused unless they are listed.

6
00:00:22,931 --> 00:00:25,358
Emergency numbers can never be added.

7
00:00:25,812 --> 00:00:29,869
Enable the soft phone is a master switch for the whole site.

8
00:00:29,869 --> 00:00:35,462
Show the soft phone on the admin dashboard puts the phone button on every admin page.

9
00:00:35,915 --> 00:00:41,729
Enable the diagnostics tab adds a tab with live call quality and a microphone meter.

10
00:00:41,729 --> 00:00:44,895
Turn it on to troubleshoot, then off again.

11
00:00:45,347 --> 00:00:49,506
Recent calls to display sets how many calls the Recent tab lists.

12
00:00:49,506 --> 00:00:54,720
Default country decides the country a national number starts with, and Accent color

13
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:57,297
sets the color of the phone's buttons.

14
00:00:57,751 --> 00:00:58,823
Click Save.

15
00:00:58,823 --> 00:01:01,661
The phone now uses the chosen provider.

